 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 33,
   "y": 21,
   "text": "BUS STOP. Route 57, Portree to Uig. Next bus: 'Soon'. The timetable was last updated: 'Recently'. A handwritten note underneath says the bus has gone for a wee coffee. It is not a lie, merely an optimistic forecast."
  },
  {
   "x": 27,
   "y": 19,
   "text": "PORT RÌGH · PORTREE. 'King's Port', after King James V, who landed here in 1540 to calm the island clans down. The harbour houses were painted bright so fishermen could find their way home in the fog."
  },
  {
   "x": 10,
   "y": 20,
   "text": "RAASAY AND THE MINCH. Across the water is Raasay, and beyond is the Minch, home of the Blue Men, storm spirits who challenge sea captains to a rhyming contest. Finish the rhyme or lose your ship."
  },
  {
   "x": 33,
   "y": 34,
   "text": "AROS CENTRE. A theatre, a cinema and a gallery, with a view of the harbour. The Skye Gaelic Mod and the Highland Games are held in the village, and everyone, including the pipers, turns up in the rain."
  }
 ],
